# Bitstream stand-in for the sysclk-sla5032 model (emu/src/models/sysclk-sla5032.rs):
# the driver cuts the first 0x69 bytes, checks a Xilinx sync word after
# them and sends the rest in chunks of 250 behind 256 bytes of FF. The
# size is the model's (a unit test checks it), not the vendor file's; it
# leaves a last chunk of 151 bytes. A plain stand-in has no sync word:
# tools/emu/sysclk-sla5032.sh lays it over before its cases.
sysclk-sla5032.bit 3000
